# sweep-dlight-gpu.steps -- clustered dynamic lights and GPU lightstyles
# through the SDL_GPU backend (-gpu) against GL (#340 P5b), on demo2 with
# torches that keep their dynamic light.
#
# Since P5b -gpu runs the light cluster: R_LightCluster_Update's dispatch is
# a compute pass of rg_compute.c's (storage image unit 0 the 32x16x32
# RGBA32UI froxel grid, LightBuffer at point 8 read-only, LcParams a
# registered mirror pushed from its flushed copy), and the world and alias
# fragment stages read the grid on unit 5 and LightBuffer's lights and
# styles.  Before it, -gpu lit every dynamic light on the CPU (lightmap
# blocks rewritten each frame, the flat per-entity term on models) and GL on
# the GPU, so the two pictures could not match.  Now both cluster, and
# lightcluster_verify says by number that the grids do.
#
# THE TEST GAME.  Stock wall torches cast no dynamic light (Init_Torch calls
# makestatic); one with a targetname stays a real entity, and its flame
# model's XF_TORCH_GLOW gives it the torch dlight, radius 150.  So
# tools/mk-dlight-testgame.py writes demo2's own entity lump as
# <basedir>/dlight/maps/demo2.ent with three of the leak check's torches
# named, its cast scene's free-standing torch and barrel appended, and every
# monster dropped, since one turning between two frames of a view is a
# difference neither backend made (the docstring has the list).  Nothing is committed: build it from the retail
# data each time.  The basedir must hold data1 as a directory, or a link that
# resolves inside headless-drive.sh's sandbox (tools/mk-alias-testgame.py).
#
# Run the SAME binary both ways, with identical settings; host_framerate
# holds game time, so the torch flames and the frozen
# lightstyles land alike run to run (sweep-mirror-gpu.steps explains it):
#
#   ./tools/mk-dlight-testgame.py <basedir>
#   A="-fsaa 0 +gamma 1 +host_framerate 0.000001 -game dlight +map demo2"
#   STEPS=tools/sweep-dlight-gpu.steps ENGINE=$E ./tools/headless-drive.sh script /tmp/dl-gl <basedir> $A
#   VK_ICD_FILENAMES=<lvp_icd json> VK_LAYER_PATH=<vulkan-validation-layers>/share/vulkan/explicit_layer.d \
#       VK_KHRONOS_VALIDATION_VALIDATE_SYNC=true VK_KHRONOS_VALIDATION_ENABLE_MESSAGE_LIMIT=false \
#       STEPS=tools/sweep-dlight-gpu.steps ENGINE=$E \
#       ./tools/headless-drive.sh script /tmp/dl-gpu <basedir> -gpu +gpu_allow_software 1 +gpu_debug 1 $A
#   ./tools/dlight-diff.sh /tmp/dl-gl /tmp/dl-gpu [/tmp/dl-gpu-master]
#
# The third directory, optional, is the same sweep under -gpu on the binary
# before P5b: frame 07 must be its 07 (r_dynamic 0, where the cluster is
# valid and empty and the CPU adds nothing either).
#
# THE FRAMES, every one at r_dynamic 1, r_dlight_occlusion 1 (the cube
# shadow maps are tools/sweep-shadow-gpu.steps'), r_lightclusters 1 and r_lightclusters_models 1 unless
# it says otherwise.  "lit" is the leak check's lit scene, the named torch at
# 170 312 80 on its own wall, seen from 210 200 99 looking down at it:
#   01  lit, r_lightclusters 0: the CPU path, on both sides
#   02  lit, r_lightclusters 1: the grid
#   03  the cast scene's barrel inside the free-standing torch's light,
#       r_lightclusters_models 1: the alias consumer
#   04  the same at r_lightclusters_models 0: the flat per-entity term
#   03g 04g 03 and 04 at r_alias_gpu 1, the desktop default: the instanced
#       alias stages (AliasVert's lc_view, LightBuffer) as the consumer
#   05  the cauldron room's flames (styles 2 and 5), r_flatlightstyles 0,
#       r_gpulightstyles 1: LightStyles[] out of the light buffer
#   05f the same at r_flatlightstyles 1, so the camera is shown to see
#       styled light at all
#   06  05 at r_gpulightstyles 0: the styles baked on the CPU
#   07  lit, r_dynamic 0: the grid valid and empty, so it adds nothing to
#       the world.  With r_gpulightstyles 0 and r_lightclusters_models 0 the
#       binary before P5b draws this view the same way bar the grid, so its
#       07 is this one exactly: GPU lightstyles round a few luxels their own
#       way (1112 pixels), and the CPU per-entity term lights models from
#       dlights even at r_dynamic 0 where the empty grid does not (952
#       pixels on the barrel, the chair and the torch -- GL's behaviour,
#       which -gpu now shares)
#   08  lit, gl_flashblend 1: the grid valid and empty, blend bubbles
#   09  lit, r_fullbright 1
#   10  lit, r_scale 0.5: the froxel columns against a scaled viewport
#   11a the leak check's scene 1 (the far side of the named torch's wall)
#   11b its scene 3 (a back face in the named torch's PVS)
#   12  lit, r_dlight_occlusion 2: the cube maps drawn on both backends
#       since #340 P6b (until then R_Shadow_Prepare returned under -gpu,
#       and this was the trap frame that proved it).  Nothing in this view
#       stands between the torch and its wall, so on GL 12 is 02 exactly,
#       and -gpu's 12 must differ from its 02 as GL's does: by nothing.
#       What the maps do stop is tools/sweep-shadow-gpu.steps'.
# then a map change (demo2 again) and the lit camera's grid checked once
# more.  No frame there: the console's state after a load is the harness's
# timing (#553), not the cluster.
#
# setpos is the server's, so every camera move is made unpaused: a paused
# server never moves the player.
#
# THE NUMBERS, measured 2026-11-27 on the P5b binary, 800x600, llvmpipe GL
# (Mesa 26.2) against lavapipe -gpu with sync validation, three runs a side
# and all nine pairings, then the Tesla P4 (NVIDIA GL through SDL's offscreen
# driver against NVIDIA Vulkan, 640x480: offscreen offers no larger mode):
#
#   check                        GL vs lavapipe        Tesla P4 GL vs Vk   gate
#   PSNR, every frame but 05-06  67.5 - 80.3           76.3 - inf          42
#   PSNR, 05 05f 06              47.6 - 70.9           66.7 - 66.9         42
#   02 vs 01 changed pixels      1426 / 1427           952 / 952           10%
#   03 vs 04, 03g vs 04g         121 / 121             77 / 77             10%
#   05 vs 05f (styled light)     4581 - 4728           2958 / 2958         2000
#   07 = before P5b, 12 = 02     0, 0                  -, 0                0
#   (12 = 02 was the P5b gate's trap; since P6b it is the maps on both sides,
#   and GL's 12 vs 02 is 0 too)
#   lightcluster_verify          identical, 0 off      identical, 0 off
#
# Each run repeats itself exactly except the cauldron room (05, 05f, 06),
# which moves by up to 648 pixels run to run on either backend: where the
# frozen flame and style phase lands is the harness's timing.  The minimum
# counts are 800x600's: at 640x480 pass MIN_CHANGED=500 MIN_ALIAS=50.
#
# THE REPORTS.  REPORT-BOOT holds the boot's gpu_unrouted; REPORT-LIT (from
# 02) and REPORT-CPU (from 01) renderer_status and lightcluster_verify, real
# lights and 64 synthetic; REPORT-ALL spans 01-12; REPORT-MAP the map change.
# Each gpu_unrouted section is reset at its start.  tools/dlight-diff.sh's
# header has the checks, the thresholds and the broken builds.

sleep 20
cmd echo REPORT-BOOT-BEGIN
cmd gpu_unrouted
cmd echo REPORT-BOOT-END
cmd god
cmd notarget
cmd noclip
cmd con_notifytime 0
cmd viewsize 120
cmd crosshair 0
cmd showpause 0
cmd cl_bob 0
cmd cl_rollangle 0
cmd r_skyspeed_back 0
cmd r_skyspeed_front 0
cmd r_flatlightstyles 1
cmd r_dynamic 1
cmd gl_flashblend 0
cmd r_fullbright 0
cmd gl_torch_dlight 1
cmd r_lightclusters 1
cmd r_lightclusters_models 1
cmd r_gpulightstyles 1
cmd r_dlight_occlusion 1
cmd r_gpucull 0
cmd gl_hiz_cull 0
cmd r_ssao 0
cmd r_bloom 0
cmd r_hdr 0
cmd r_alias_gpu 0
cmd r_particles 0
cmd fog 0
cmd gl_texture_anisotropy 1
cmd r_oit 0
cmd r_waterwarp 0
cmd r_motionblur 0
cmd r_softparticles 0
cmd r_softemu 0
cmd r_scale 1
cmd gl_fxaa 0
cmd contrast 1
cmd gl_waterwarp_speed 0
cmd r_caustics 0
cmd gl_glows 0
cmd gl_missile_glows 0
cmd gl_other_glows 0
cmd r_drawviewmodel 0
cmd r_drawentities 1
cmd r_pp_time 10
sleep 2

cmd setpos 210 200 99 20 90 0
sleep 2
cmd gpu_unrouted reset
cmd pause
cmd r_lightclusters 0
shot 01-lit-cpu
cmd echo REPORT-CPU-BEGIN
cmd gpu_unrouted
cmd renderer_status
cmd echo REPORT-CPU-END
cmd r_lightclusters 1
shot 02-lit-gpu
cmd echo REPORT-LIT-BEGIN
cmd renderer_status
cmd lightcluster_verify
cmd lightcluster_verify 64
cmd gpu_unrouted
cmd echo REPORT-LIT-END

cmd pause
cmd setpos 120 150 100 25 90 0
sleep 2
cmd pause
shot 03-cast-models
cmd r_lightclusters_models 0
shot 04-cast-nomodels
cmd r_lightclusters_models 1
cmd r_alias_gpu 1
shot 03g-cast-models-inst
cmd r_lightclusters_models 0
shot 04g-cast-nomodels-inst
cmd r_lightclusters_models 1
cmd r_alias_gpu 0

cmd pause
cmd setpos 632 40 300 15 90 0
sleep 2
cmd pause
cmd r_flatlightstyles 0
shot 05-styles-gpu
cmd r_flatlightstyles 1
shot 05f-styles-flat
cmd r_flatlightstyles 0
cmd r_gpulightstyles 0
shot 06-styles-cpu
cmd r_gpulightstyles 1
cmd r_flatlightstyles 1

cmd pause
cmd setpos 210 200 99 20 90 0
sleep 2
cmd pause
cmd r_gpulightstyles 0
cmd r_lightclusters_models 0
cmd r_dynamic 0
shot 07-lit-dynamic0
cmd r_dynamic 1
cmd r_lightclusters_models 1
cmd r_gpulightstyles 1
cmd gl_flashblend 1
shot 08-lit-flashblend
cmd gl_flashblend 0
cmd r_fullbright 1
shot 09-lit-fullbright
cmd r_fullbright 0
cmd r_scale 0.5
shot 10-lit-scale050
cmd r_scale 1

cmd pause
cmd setpos -830 32 150 0 -90 0
sleep 2
cmd pause
shot 11a-leak1
cmd pause
cmd setpos -811 1088 247 17 -90 0
sleep 2
cmd pause
shot 11b-leak3

cmd pause
cmd setpos 210 200 99 20 90 0
sleep 2
cmd pause
cmd r_dlight_occlusion 2
shot 12-lit-occl2
cmd r_dlight_occlusion 1
cmd echo REPORT-ALL-BEGIN
cmd gpu_unrouted
cmd renderer_status
cmd echo REPORT-ALL-END

cmd pause
cmd gpu_unrouted reset
console
enter map demo2
sleep 25
cmd echo REPORT-MAP-BEGIN
cmd setpos 210 200 99 20 90 0
sleep 2
cmd lightcluster_verify 64
cmd renderer_status
cmd gpu_unrouted
cmd echo REPORT-MAP-END
sleep 1
